Remove msi-ec debug mode (the debug module parameter).

With debug=1 the driver exported /sys/devices/platform/msi-ec/debug/:
ec_set writes any value to any of the embedded controller's 256 registers,
ec_get and ec_dump read any of them, and the driver also loaded on
unsupported or banned firmware. A signed module must not give root raw
hardware register writes, which lockdown exists to remove (the kernel's
ec_sys write support goes through debugfs, which lockdown restricts).
The fixed-function attributes are unchanged; fw_version stays in the root
group.

--- a/msi-ec.c
+++ b/msi-ec.c
@@ -1671,9 +1671,6 @@
 module_param(firmware, charp, 0);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(firmware, "Load a configuration for a specified firmware version");
 
-static bool debug = false;
-module_param(debug, bool, 0);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(debug, "Load the driver in the debug mode, exporting the debug attributes");
 
